meta {
  name: Get Placer Token (L1, client_secret debug client)
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
  body: formUrlEncoded
  auth: none
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  grant_type: client_credentials
  client_id: {{placerL1ClientId}}
  client_secret: {{placerL1ClientSecret}}
  scope: system/Task.crus system/ServiceRequest.rs system/Patient.r
}

docs {
  L1 (`client_secret`) is an explicit, per-hospital **opt-in debug client** (ADR 0004, docs/adr/0004-reinstate-l1-debug-client.md) — not the production path. It exists so a hospital can confirm basic connectivity and routing (firewalls, proxies) before or instead of standing up the full L2 `private_key_jwt` flow, which is harder to isolate through those same failure modes.

  This request only works if `keycloak-config/clients/hospital_a-l1.yaml` is present (it is not, by default — see the README in that directory) and `terraform apply` has since run with `allow_l1_debug_clients=true` (default `false` — see below). Unlike L2, the client secret is Keycloak-generated, not a demo key checked into this repo — fetch it with:

    terraform output -json m2m_l1_client_secrets | jq -r '.["hospital_a-l1"]'

  and set `placerL1ClientSecret` in the `local` Bruno environment (or as a runtime override). No pre-request signing script is needed — `client_id` + `client_secret` is a plain grant, so this request works in either Bruno sandbox (QuickJS or Node.js).

  Resulting tokens carry `extensions.umzhconnect.auth_level = "L1"` (vs. `"L2"` for the standard client) so resource servers can distinguish and, if desired, reject L1 tokens for real clinical data flows.

  `terraform apply` creates this client (and any other L1 client) only when `allow_l1_debug_clients=true` (`variables.tf`, default `false`), in every environment including local `docker-compose`. When it's `false`, `keycloak-config/clients/hospital_a-l1.yaml` is silently ignored — apply still succeeds, but only logs a warning, and this request will 400/401 since the client was never created. Run `TF_VAR_allow_l1_debug_clients=true docker compose up keycloak-config` (or `docker compose run --rm -e TF_VAR_allow_l1_debug_clients=true keycloak-config` for a guaranteed one-off apply) before this request will work locally — see [ai-docs/infrastructure.md](../../ai-docs/infrastructure.md) ("Enabling L1 debug clients locally") for the "Compose ignores unreferenced host env vars" and "container already up to date" gotchas.
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.access_token: isDefined
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 200) {
    bru.setVar("placerL1Token", res.getBody().access_token);
  }
}
